[38;5;252m[1m## Verification[0m[0m
[0m[0m
I built the C reference the way the shipped [38;5;10mCMakeLists.txt[0m does and diffed stdout, stderr, the interleaved merge, and exit codes: 30 hand-written edge cases plus ~3200 randomized command scripts, all byte-identical.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Bugs reproduced rather than fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mdelete_node[0m frees a node but leaves the dangling pointer in [38;5;10mgraph->nodes[0m, so listing shows freed nodes and a later "add city" recycles that exact chunk, making one node appear twice. Nodes therefore live in an arena indexed by simulated glibc chunk addresses, with LIFO size-binned recycling.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mfree()[0m overwrites the first 8 bytes of a freed chunk with glibc's safe-linked [38;5;10mnext[0m pointer, which aliases [38;5;10mcity_name[0m â€” so a freed node prints a short garbage name that matches no lookup. I reproduce the [38;5;10m(ptr >> 12) ^ next[0m computation.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mshallow_copy[0m can resurrect an already-freed node's refcount, so program exit hits a genuine double free. I emit glibc's exact [38;5;10mfree(): double free detected in tcache 2[0m and [38;5;10mabort()[0m, discarding unflushed stdout.[0m[0m
- Names truncate to 63 bytes on store but are echoed untruncated, [38;5;10mINT_MAX[0m sentinel distances are unreachable in the Dijkstra frontier, distance sums wrap on overflow, and [38;5;10mfgets[0m returning NULL inside a case breaks only the [38;5;10mswitch[0m, printing the menu one extra time.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Two things worth knowing[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The C is only deterministic here with ASLR disabled. Under normal ASLR the freed-chunk bytes are random and the C binary disagrees with itself run to run; my model matches the ASLR-off reference exactly and cannot be matched by anything under ASLR-on. I noted this in the code.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Separately, the double free is masked at [38;5;10m-O0[0m (the shipped CMake config, no [38;5;10mCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE[0m) but fires at [38;5;10m-O1[0m and above, where dead-store elimination drops the [38;5;10mref_count[0m decrement into freed memory and every delete-to-zero aborts with empty stdout. I targeted the shipped configuration.[0m[0m
